{"abstract":[{"text":"Six small programs that show how the pieces fit together, and that you can run.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/Examples"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"NanoHTTP"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Examples"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The package has six executable targets in its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Examples","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" folder. Every one is a complete program of one or two pages,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with comments that say why things are done the way they are; start the one that is closest to what you want to build","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and change it. They are Swift package targets: in Xcode, choose the package scheme of the example, or run them from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"command line:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["swift run ExampleHello","swift run ExampleTodoAPI --port 9000","swift run ExampleFileServer --directory ~/Downloads"],"syntax":"bash","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"All of them listen at the loopback address, so only programs on your machine can connect, and say where they listen. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"options are the same everywhere: ","type":"text"},{"code":"--port 8080","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" picks a free port) and ","type":"text"},{"code":"--network","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which makes the server reachable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from other devices (on a network that you trust). Ctrl-C stops the server: the examples use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoProcess/watchSignals(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to stop it, so that the program ends normally.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Example","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"What it shows","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ExampleHello","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The smallest useful server: routes, a route variable, a query parameter, a body, a page for unknown paths.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ExampleTodoAPI","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A JSON API: ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" models in and out (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPResponse/json(_:status:headers:encoder:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPRequest/json(_:decoder:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"), status codes (","type":"text"},{"code":"201","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Location","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"204","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"422","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), errors as JSON (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer/errorHandler","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"), middleware, and a lock around the state that the handlers share.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ExampleFileServer","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A directory on the web: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoFiles/share(directory:defaults:followSymlinks:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoFiles/browse(directory:followSymlinks:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and the Host and Origin policies that keep web pages of other sites away.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ExampleChat","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A chat room: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoWebSocket","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoWebSocketHub","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" that sends to all sessions, a page built with NanoHTML, and the origin check for the WebSocket.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ExampleStatus","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A server with ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one thread","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/Threading-swift.enum/singleThread","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"): counters that are plain variables, no locks, and a live display over a WebSocket.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ExampleUpload","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A form with a file upload: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPRequest/parseMultiPartFormData()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", the limits of the server, cookies (a message that is shown once), and post/redirect/get with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPResponse/seeOther(_:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Everything that a request contains is treated as untrusted in them: pages escape it (NanoHTML does that for you),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"file names are only displayed, and the limits of the server are set for what the example needs. Read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/SecurityAndLimits","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" before you put a server of your own where others can reach it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Checking-the-examples","level":2,"text":"Checking the examples","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"python3 Scripts/check_examples.py","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" builds the examples, starts every one on a free port, makes real requests (including","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"WebSocket handshakes) and stops it with ","type":"text"},{"code":"SIGTERM","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"--sanitize=thread","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does the same with the thread sanitizer. It is how the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"examples are kept working.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP":{"abstract":[{"text":"A small HTTP/1.1 server for apps and tools: routing, files, forms, uploads and WebSockets, without dependencies.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"NanoHTTP","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/GettingStarted":{"abstract":[{"text":"Add NanoHTTP to a project, answer your first request and learn where to go next.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/GettingStarted","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Getting Started","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/gettingstarted"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/Handler